RUN 2 (cfe36efe-e981-4531-8c78-1e4d48e8c11c, session 143ef294-...):
  Same arrival; DIAG DOM dump proved the app DID hydrate — onboarding step 1
  ("Bienvenue sur Hamame", "Étape 1 sur 4", "Plus tard") rendered in place of
  the player. "Plus tard" click did not clear the gate across navigations.

RUN 3 (da322376-0291-485f-a6cb-ca74690cc4ca, session 0c626225-...):
  Skip-loop retry also stuck at step 1.

Root cause found in code:
  web/src/lib/useRequireAuth.ts:42 — signed-in user missing faculty/year is
  router.replace("/bienvenue")-ed; skip() only sets localStorage
  "hamame_onboarding_skip" on the /bienvenue page itself. The /bienvenue
  finish() flow does PUT /api/users/me {facultyId, yearId} (page.tsx:101-107).

RUN 4 (ceb9f14e-76b1-4430-b0c3-6f60e5a377bb, session eb37bea3-...):
  Added onboarding completion via API (PUT /users/me with fixture faculty/year)
  before opening the browser. Failed at the response shape:

    === 3b. finish onboarding via API (fixture faculty/year) ===
    E2E-FAIL Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'id')

  Cause: PUT /api/users/me returns the user object DIRECTLY
  (src/routes/users.routes.ts:176 res.status(200).json(user)) — the harness
  destructured `{ user }`. Fixed.

  HARNESS BUG (disclosed): because of how the 3b patch was anchored, the
  state-file write-back ended up AFTER the 3b block in web/tmp-e2e-explain.mjs
  — so RUN 4 (which threw at 3b) never persisted its user/session IDs into
  the cleanup state file. Its session was still caught by cleanup's
  sessionQuestion-join sweep (5 sessions deleted), but its USER ROW survived
  the first cleanup — see §6 for the explicit audit + removal.

